			"notes": "First release.\n\n**Install**\n1. Make a **Fabric** instance for Minecraft **26.3** in your launcher (Freesm, Prism or the official one) and put `meetcraft-0.1.0.jar` in its `mods/` folder. It's the only mod you need: Fabric API and Plasmo Voice are built in.\n2. In **Firefox** or another Firefox-based browser (Zen, LibreWolf, Floorp…, version 128 or newer), open `meetcraft-0.1.0.xpi` and click *Add*. Chrome, Edge and Brave aren't supported.\n3. Join the call in Google Meet. The \"⛏ MeetCraft\" badge on the Meet page shows when Minecraft is connected.\n\nThe full guide is in the [README](https://github.com/hunortakacs/meetcraft#readme)."
		}
